-- erwartet: H022
-- **A self-call without a descent measure (must fall).**
--
-- `f` reaches itself and declares no `decreases`. On a cycle every edge counts the
-- DECLARED `costs` of the callee once, so the promise is an assumption, not a result.
-- `K008` refuses the bare member (the self-recursive shape on its own stands in
-- `gift/150`); `H022` names the cycle as one composition unit. `K001` fires beside
-- them: the self-call counts the DECLARED `costs` (8), so the body (13) exceeds its
-- own promise -- on a bare member that over-count is structural (`kosten.rs`: a
-- recursive call costs nothing only under `decreases`). The mutual shape is
-- `gift/746`, the three-member shape `gift/748`.
module gift::selbstruf_ohne_mass {

static mut a : u32 = 0;

impl fn f(n : u32) -> u32 effects { writes a } costs <= 8 ops
{ a = n; if n == 0 { return 0; } return f(n); }

}
